normalForm -- computes the normal form within the rational Weyl algebra
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        normalForm(P, Q)
        normalForm(P, G)
  * Inputs:
      * P, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, in the Weyl
        algebra
      * Q, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, in the Weyl
        algebra
      * G, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of elements in the Weyl algebra
        (typically a Gröbner basis of a $D_n$-ideal)
  * Outputs:
      * normalForm, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,,
        normalForm, computed in rational Weyl algebra with respect to a list of
        elements in the Weyl algebra

Description
===========

This method computes the normal form of an element $P$ in the Weyl algebra
$D_n$ with respect to another element in the Weyl algebra, or a whole list of
such elements. The reduction step is carried out over the rational Weyl algebra
$R_n$.

+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : D = makeWeylAlgebra(QQ[x,y], {1,1});|
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : P = dx^2 ; Q = x*dx+1;              |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i4 : normalForm(P, Q)                    |
|                                         |
|      2                                  |
|o4 = --                                  |
|      2                                  |
|     x                                   |
|                                         |
|o4 : frac(QQ[x..y])[dx, dy]              |
+-----------------------------------------+

We can compute the normal form with respect to the Gröbner basis of a
$D$-ideal.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : D = makeWeylAlgebra(QQ[x, y]);                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : I = ideal(x*dx^2-y*dy^2+2*dx-2*dy, x*dx+y*dy+1);|
|                                                     |
|o6 : Ideal of D                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : G = first entries mingens gb I;                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : P = dx;                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : normalForm(P,G)                                 |
|                                                     |
|       y      1                                      |
|o9 = - -*dy - -                                      |
|       x      x                                      |
|                                                     |
|o9 : frac(QQ[x..y])[dx, dy]                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

References
==========

See [SST (see https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-662-04112-3 ),
Theorem 1.1.7].

Caveat
======

Due to technical limitations, the output lives in the graded associative
algebra of the rational Weyl algebra, which is a commutative ring over the
*note base fraction field: baseFractionField, of $D_n$ where the partial
differentials are adjoined as commuting variables.

Ways to use normalForm:
=======================

  * "normalForm(RingElement,List)"
  * "normalForm(RingElement,RingElement)"
  * normalForm(RingElement,GroebnerBasis) (missing documentation)

