gaugeMatrix -- computes the base change over the field of rational functions
****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        gaugeMatrix(G, B)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, of the Weyl algebra
      * G, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of generators of a Gröbner basis
        for $I$
      * B, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of standard monomials for $I$,
        i.e. any basis of $R_n/R_nI$ over the field of rational functions
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, encoding the change of basis
        with regard to to $B$

Description
===========

Let $I = D_n\langle G\rangle$ be a $D_n$-ideal, $B$ basis of $R_n/R_nI$. This
methods computes the matrix which encodes the change of basis from the set of
standard monomials of $R_nI$ to the basis $B$.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D1 = makeWeylAlgebra(QQ[x, y], w1 = {2, 1});    |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x*dx^2-y*dy^2+2*dx-2*dy, x*dx+y*dy+1);|
|                                                     |
|o2 : Ideal of D1                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : SM1 = standardMonomials I                       |
|                                                     |
|o3 = {1, dy}                                         |
|                                                     |
|o3 : List                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : F = baseFractionField D1;                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : D2 = makeWeylAlgebra(QQ[x, y], w2 = {1, 2});    |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : SM2 = standardMonomials sub(I, D2)              |
|                                                     |
|o6 = {1, dx}                                         |
|                                                     |
|o6 : List                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : gaugeMatrix(I, SM2)                             |
|                                                     |
|o7 = | 1    0    |                                   |
|     | -1/x -y/x |                                   |
|                                                     |
|             2      2                                |
|o7 : Matrix F  <-- F                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

It is also possible to compute the gauge matrix of a system of connection
matrices containing parameters.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : D = makeWeylAlgebra(frac(QQ[a])[x]);           |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : I = ideal(x^2*dx^2 + x*dx + (x^2-a^2))         |
|                                                    |
|            2  2           2    2                   |
|o9 = ideal(x dx  + x*dx + x  - a )                  |
|                                                    |
|o9 : Ideal of D                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : standardMonomials I                           |
|                                                    |
|o10 = {1, dx}                                       |
|                                                    |
|o10 : List                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : gaugeMatrix(I,{dx,x^2*dx^2+x*dx+x^2})         |
|                                                    |
|o11 = | 0  1 |                                      |
|      | a2 0 |                                      |
