File: ConnectionMatrices.info, Node: gaugeTransform, Next: isEpsilonFactorized, Prev: gaugeMatrix, Up: Top

gaugeTransform -- computes the gauge transform of a system of connection matrices
*********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        gaugeTransform(M, A, D)
        gaugeTransform(M, A)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, change of basis matrix
      * A, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a system of connection matrices
      * D, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the Weyl algebra (if omitted, it
        will be inferred from first element of A)
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the system of connection matrices
        $\widetilde{A}_i = M A_i M^{-1} + (\partial_i \bullet M)M^{-1}$ after
        the gauge transformation with respect to $M$.

Description
===========

This method computes the gauge transform of a system of connection matrices for
a given invertible matrix that encodes a change of basis.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D = makeWeylAlgebra(QQ[x,y]);                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x*dx^2-y*dy^2+2*dx-2*dy, x*dx+y*dy+1);|
|                                                     |
|o2 : Ideal of D                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : A = pfaffianSystem I;                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : M = matrix {{x,0}, {0,y}};                      |
|                                                     |
|             2      2                                |
|o4 : Matrix D  <-- D                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : gaugeTransform(M, A, D)                         |
|                                                     |
|o5 = {| 0 -1 |, | 0 x/y  |}                          |
|      | 0 0  |  | 0 -1/y |                           |
|                                                     |
|o5 : List                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

It is also possible to compute the gauge transform of a system of connection
matrices containing parameters.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : D = makeWeylAlgebra(frac(QQ[a])[x]);          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : I = ideal(x^2*dx^2 + x*dx + (x^2-a^2))        |
|                                                   |
|            2  2           2    2                  |
|o7 = ideal(x dx  + x*dx + x  - a )                 |
|                                                   |
|o7 : Ideal of D                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : A = pfaffianSystem I                          |
|                                                   |
|o8 = {| 0           1    |}                        |
|      | (-x2+a2)/x2 -1/x |                         |
|                                                   |
|o8 : List                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : M = gaugeMatrix(I,{dx,x^2*dx^2+x*dx+x^2});    |
|                                                   |
|                            2                     2|
|o9 : Matrix (frac(QQ[x, a]))  <-- (frac(QQ[x, a])) |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : gaugeTransform(M,A)                          |
|                                                   |
|o10 = {| -1/x (-x2+a2)/x2a2 |}                     |
|       | a2   0             |                      |
|                                                   |
|o10 : List                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------+

See *note Cosmological correlator for the 2-site chain: Cosmological correlator
for the 2-site chain, for an example.

