isEpsilonFactorized -- checks whether a system of connection matrices is in $\epsilon$-factorized form
******************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isEpsilonFactorized(A,eps)
        isEpsilonFactorized(M,eps)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a system of connection matrices
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a connection matrix
      * eps, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, parameter for
        which the factorization property should be tested
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true or false

Description
===========

This method returns true if the system of connection matrices factors out (a
power of) eps, such that the resulting matrices are independent of eps.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D = makeWeylAlgebra(frac(QQ[ϵ])[x]); |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x*(1-x)*dx^2 - ϵ*(1-x)*dx);|
|                                          |
|o2 : Ideal of D                           |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : A = pfaffianSystem(I)                |
|                                          |
|o3 = {| 0 1   |}                          |
|      | 0 ϵ/x |                           |
|                                          |
|o3 : List                                 |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isEpsilonFactorized(A, ϵ)            |
|                                          |
|o4 = false                                |
+------------------------------------------+

The property of being epsilon factorizable depends on a choice of basis.

+-----------------------------------------+
|i5 : A = pfaffianSystem(I, {1_D, 1/ϵ*dx})|
|                                         |
|o5 = {| 0 ϵ   |}                         |
|      | 0 ϵ/x |                          |
|                                         |
|o5 : List                                |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i6 : isEpsilonFactorized(A, ϵ)           |
|                                         |
|o6 = true                                |
+-----------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note isIntegrable: isIntegrable, -- checks whether a list of matrices
    fulfills the integrability conditions
  * *note gaugeTransform: gaugeTransform, -- computes the gauge transform of a
    system of connection matrices

